<blockquote class="uncited"><div> I recall stressing it should be such axis whose length in radians corresponds to the rate of spin/angular velocity.</div></blockquote>I recall making the same argument myself.  sigh.  <br><br>I just checked the Maya import and export implementation and unfortunately the code there looks like it scales the magnitude of the spin vector by 180/pi on export and back again on import.   So it looks like we have different interpretations of the schema after all.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>There might be some other inconsistencies. </div></blockquote>Indeed.  In addition to clarification in the docs (spec), some design (schema) fixes will be needed.  The consequence of not doing so is evident in the lack of consistency amongst the different implementations.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=483">melax</a> — Sat Feb 09, 2008 2:58 am</p><hr />
